<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>HTML Lists with CSS</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial;background:#f2f2f2;padding:10px}
h1{text-align:center;color:#1a237e;margin:2px}
.roll{text-align:center;color:#d84315;font-weight:bold;margin:2px}
h2{color:#d84315;margin:2px}
.box{background:white;padding:8px;margin:5px auto;width:70%;border-radius:5px;box-shadow:0 0 3px gray}
p{margin:2px 0}
ul,ol{margin:2px 0;font-size:16px}
ul{color:green}
ol{color:blue}
dl{margin:2px 0}
dt{color:purple;font-weight:bold}
dd{color:#555;margin:1px 0}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Working of HTML Lists</h1>
<div class="roll">Roll Number: 25K65A1203</div>
<div class="box">
<h2>1. Unordered List</h2>
<p>An unordered list displays items using bullets.</p>
<ul>
<li>Apple</li>
<li>Banana</li>
<li>Mango</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="box">
<h2>2. Ordered List</h2>
<p>An ordered list displays items using numbers.</p>
<ol>
<li>Wake up</li>
<li>Brush Teeth</li>
<li>Go to School</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="box">
<h2>3. Description List</h2>
<p>A description list contains terms and their descriptions.</p>
<dl>
<dt>HTML</dt>
<dd>Used to create web pages.</dd>
<dt>CSS</dt>
<dd>Used to style web pages.</dd>
<dt>JavaScript</dt>
<dd>Used to make web pages interactive.</dd>
</dl>
</div>
</body>
</html>
